import SharpRangeCert
import FormMuMax

/-!
# The maximal slope of the source from integral coordinates

A reduction of the bound on `μ_max(M_ω)` for the range (R′) (`ZetaBalance.SharpMuMax`, in `SharpRangeCert`) to a
statement about the forms alone: integral coordinates on the source, dominated by the Petersson form
(`ZetaBalance.sharpMuMax_of_coordCert`). All slopes are in the archive's units.

**Integral coordinates** (`SharpObj.CoordCert`). For a word `ω`, a `K`-linear `T : V_ω → K^J` is a set of integral
coordinates of weight `w > 0` if it is injective, takes integral values on the integral forms (the generators of
`M_ω`), and `w·Σ_j |Σ_i y_i·σ_v(T f_i)_j|² ≤ Σ_{i,i'} conj(y_i)·H_{σ_v}(f_i, f_{i'})·y_{i'}` for every finite family
`f_i ∈ V_ω`, complex coefficients `y_i` and complex place `v`: the Petersson form `H_{σ_v}` (`HermForms.petAt`)
dominates `w·|σ_v ∘ T|²` on `V_ω ⊗_{σ_v} ℂ`.

**The bound** (`SharpObj.muMaxLe_of_coordCert`). If every word has integral coordinates of weight `w`, then
`μ_max(M_ω) ≤ −log w` in every realising frame (`SharpObj.MuMaxLe`). In the frame's coordinates `c_ω` the source's
metric at `v` is the Gram matrix of `H_{σ_v}` (`SharpObj.RealWith`), so `T ∘ c_ω⁻¹` meets the hypotheses of
`KLattice.slopeLe_of_coord`: integral on `M_ω`, the `O_K`-span of the integral forms, as the integral elements of
`K` are an `O_K`-module; and dominated by the metric, taking `f_i = c_ω⁻¹(e_i)`. `M_ω` is an `O_K`-lattice
(`HermForms.isLattice_span_Mω`), for antitone weights.

**The construction** (`sharpMuMax_of_coordCert`). `SharpMuMax` follows from `SharpCoordCert`: eventually in the
design, at each translate, integral coordinates of some weight `w` with `−log w + c_F^{exact} ≤ x^{4ε}Σ_t a_t/8`.

**What remains.** `SharpCoordCert` is not proved. The natural coordinates are the coefficients of the values at
class representatives, `F ↦ coeff_d F(rep c)`: by `HermForms.gram_eq` the Petersson form is
`Σ_{c,d} mass(c)·d!/κ·|coeff_d F(rep c)|²`, so their weight is `1/(κ·max_c |Stab c|)`; `log κ`, the log of the
product of the hook lengths of `ν` (`FockNorm.kapN_formula`), is at most `|ν|·log|ν| ≤ 2A·log 2A`, `A = Σ_t a_t`,
within the budget as `log A ≈ x^ε`. But they are integral only up to a denominator that depends on the
representative: `F(rep c) ∈ Δ_{Lsh(rep c)}` is integral in the coordinates of local bases of `Lsh(rep c)`
(`WeylSandwich.Delta_subset_nablaInt`), and the standard monomials see `Lsh(rep c)` only through
`a·O_E^n ⊆ Lsh(rep c) ⊆ b⁻¹O_E^n` (`HermForms.Sand`), at a cost of about `a^{|ν|}`, with `|ν|` up to `2A`. The
representatives range over all classes of unimodular hermitian lattices of rank `k`, so the coordinates need
`log a ≪ x^{4ε}` uniformly in the class: a reduction theory of those lattices polynomial in `k`, for instance
functionals built from bideterminants in a basis of short vectors of `Lsh(rep c)`. Alternatively, `μ_max(M_ω)`
should be bounded without coordinates. Conjugated by an automorphism of `K` that induces complex conjugation at
`σ_v` (`K` is normal), the Petersson pairing is integral on the integral forms up to the stabilisers and the level
at `ST`: the conjugate of `Δ_X` is `Δ_{conj X}`, and the bilinear Fock pairing of `Δ_{conj X}` with `∇_{X^#}` is
integral, `X^#` being the bilinear dual of `conj X`. But `K` is not CM, and that automorphism depends on `v`, so the
product formula applies only to sublattices defined over the CM subfield generated by `τ(E)` and the values of the
character; a maximal destabilising sublattice is one, being stable under the Galois group of `K` over that subfield
(supermodularity of the degree).
-/

open NumberField HermitianLattice

namespace ZetaBalance

attribute [local instance] InnerProductSpace.complexToReal

namespace SharpObj

variable {S : Setting} {κ : S.A →* ℂˣ} {x ε X : ℝ} {Dg : SharpDesign S κ x ε X} {C : SharpCoeff S}
  (b : SharpObj Dg C)

/-- **Integral coordinates of weight `w`** on the source of a word `ω`: a `K`-linear `T : V_ω → K^J`, injective,
integral on the integral forms, with `w·|σ_v(T)(Σ_i y_i f_i)|² ≤ H_{σ_v}(Σ_i y_i f_i, Σ_i y_i f_i)` for every finite
family `f_i` of `V_ω`, complex coefficients `y_i` and complex place `v`. -/
def CoordCert (ω : b.Ω) {J : Type} [Fintype J] (T : b.Vs ω →ₗ[C.K] (J → C.K)) (w : ℝ) : Prop :=
  Function.Injective T ∧
    (∀ φ, (b.e ω φ).1 ∈ HermForms.Mω (b.ST ω) C.τK (b.χ0 ω) (b.lam0 ω) → ∀ j, T φ j ∈ (1 : Submodule (𝓞 C.K) C.K)) ∧
    ∀ (v : Pl C.K) (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] (f : ι → b.Vs ω) (y : ι → ℂ),
      w * ∑ j, ‖∑ i, v.1.embedding (T (f i) j) * y i‖ ^ 2 ≤
        (∑ i, ∑ i', starRingEnd ℂ (y i) * HermForms.petAt (b.ST ω) (b.lam0 ω) v.1.embedding (b.e ω (f i)).1
          (b.e ω (f i')).1 * y i').re

/-- **The maximal slope of `M_ω` from integral coordinates**: if the weights are antitone and every word has
integral coordinates of weight `w > 0` (`CoordCert`), then `μ_max(M_ω) ≤ −log w` in every realising frame. In the
frame's coordinates `c_ω`, `T ∘ c_ω⁻¹` is integral on `M_ω` and dominated by the source's metric, the Gram matrix of
the Petersson form (`RealWith`), so `KLattice.slopeLe_of_coord` applies. -/
theorem muMaxLe_of_coordCert (hlam : ∀ ω ρ, Antitone (b.lam0 ω ρ)) {w : ℝ} (hw : 0 < w)
    (hc : ∀ ω, ∃ (J : Type) (_ : Fintype J) (T : b.Vs ω →ₗ[C.K] (J → C.K)), b.CoordCert ω T w) :
    b.MuMaxLe (-Real.log w) := by
  classical
  intro F c eC hF ω
  obtain ⟨J, _, T, hTinj, hTM, hTG⟩ := hc ω
  have := HermForms.finiteDimensional_Vω (b.ST ω) C.τK (b.χ0 ω) (b.lam0 ω) (hlam ω)
  have hM : (b.M ω).IsLattice C.K :=
    HermForms.isLattice_span_Mω (b.ST ω) C.τK (b.χ0 ω) (b.lam0 ω) (hlam ω) (b.e ω)
  set f := (c ω : b.Vs ω →ₗ[C.K] (F.n ω → C.K)).restrictScalars (𝓞 C.K)
  have hL : ((b.M ω).map f).IsLattice C.K := ⟨hM.fg.map _, by
    rw [Submodule.map_coe, LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars, Submodule.span_image, hM.span_eq_top, Submodule.map_top,
      LinearEquiv.range]⟩
  refine ⟨hL, ?_⟩
  -- `T` is integral on `M_ω`, the `O_K`-span of the integral forms
  have hTM' (ψ : b.Vs ω) (hψ : ψ ∈ b.M ω) : ∀ j, T ψ j ∈ (1 : Submodule (𝓞 C.K) C.K) := by
    induction hψ using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem ψ hψ => exact hTM ψ hψ
    | zero =>
      intro j
      rw [map_zero]
      exact zero_mem _
    | add ψ χ _ _ h h' =>
      intro j
      rw [map_add]
      exact add_mem (h j) (h' j)
    | smul k ψ _ h =>
      intro j
      rw [← algebraMap_smul C.K k ψ, map_smul]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ k (h j)
  refine KLattice.slopeLe_of_coord ((F.src ω).withLattice ((b.M ω).map f)) (T ∘ₗ (c ω).symm.toLinearMap)
    (hTinj.comp (c ω).symm.injective) (fun y hy j => ?_) hw fun v y => ?_
  · obtain ⟨ψ, hψ, rfl⟩ := hy
    have : (c ω).symm (f ψ) = ψ := (c ω).symm_apply_apply ψ
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, this]
    exact hTM' ψ hψ j
  · simp only [hF.2.2.2.2.1 ω v]
    exact hTG v (F.n ω) (fun i => (c ω).symm (Pi.single i 1)) y

end SharpObj

/-- **Integral coordinates within the budget**, eventually in the design: at every admissible design with `ε` small
and `x` large, at every translate `u ∈ A₀`, some `w > 0` with `−log w + c_F^{exact} ≤ x^{4ε}Σ_t a_t/8` is the weight
of integral coordinates (`SharpObj.CoordCert`) on the source of every word of the construction. -/
def SharpCoordCert : Prop :=
  EventuallyAdm (fun Dg => Dg.Adm) fun {S κ x ε X} (Dg : SharpDesign S κ x ε X) => ∀ u ∈ A₀ κ, ∃ w : ℝ, 0 < w ∧
    -Real.log w + HermForms.cFx Dg.R.k (sharpLam0 Dg u) (sharpST Dg u) ≤ x ^ (4 * ε) * (∑ s ∈ Dg.TT, Dg.a s) / 8 ∧
      ∀ ω, ∃ (J : Type) (_ : Fintype J)
        (T : ((sharpCons Dg).obj u).Vs ω →ₗ[(sharpCons Dg).C.K] (J → (sharpCons Dg).C.K)),
        ((sharpCons Dg).obj u).CoordCert ω T w

/-- **The bound on `μ_max(M_ω)` from integral coordinates** (`SharpMuMax`): at the same designs, `B = −log w`
(`SharpObj.muMaxLe_of_coordCert`, with the antitone step-0 weights `Setting.Ranks.wt0_antitone`). -/
theorem sharpMuMax_of_coordCert (h : SharpCoordCert) : SharpMuMax := by
  obtain ⟨ε₁, hε₁, H⟩ := h
  refine ⟨ε₁, hε₁, fun ε hε hle => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ := H ε hε hle
  refine ⟨x₀, fun {S κ x X} Dg hx hA u hu => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hB, hc⟩ := hx₀ Dg hx hA u hu
  exact ⟨-Real.log w, hB,
    ((sharpCons Dg).obj u).muMaxLe_of_coordCert (fun _ _ => Setting.Ranks.wt0_antitone _ _ _) hw hc⟩

end ZetaBalance
